text:
maria: heads-up: onboarding team hit a nasty DX issue — duplicated request ids and inconsistent redaction between SDKs during developer trials. created thread so we can sync quickly.

trent: saw this too. reproduction steps: use sample-apps/node-onboard to send a request with `email: test@example.com` in the JSON body. node sdk logs show email redacted, but otlp spans contain the raw email in `http.request.body` attribute.

li: quick note: python SDK attaches request id to structlog via `req_id` key, but node uses `x-request-id` header only. downstream tooling (sentry, datadog) expects `request_id` attribute.

maria: proposed fixes: (1) unify on `request_id` as the canonical key across SDKs and put it into OTEL baggage+span attribute, (2) run redaction on all telemetry sinks (logs, span attrs, exported OTLP payloads) with same rule set, (3) add `telemetry.pre_process_span` hook for custom pipelines.

trent: example node middleware: 
```js
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const rid = req.headers['x-request-id'] || uuid.v4();
  req.request_id = rid;
  // set on span when available
  const span = tracer.getCurrentSpan();
  if (span) span.setAttribute('request_id', rid);
  res.setHeader('x-request-id', rid);
  next();
});
```

li: python snippet for fastapi to bind to structlog and otel baggage: 
```py
async def middleware(request, call_next):
  rid = request.headers.get('x-request-id') or str(uuid.uuid4())
  baggage.set_baggage('request_id', rid)
  structlog.threadlocal.bind_threadlocal(request_id=rid)
  resp = await call_next(request)
  resp.headers['x-request-id'] = rid
  return resp
```

ryan: agree on `request_id`. for redaction rules we should default to a small conservative set: emails, credit_card, ssn, api_keys. provide regex and key blocklist. also we need tests: unit for SDK-level redaction, and integration to assert exported otlp doesn't leak PII.

telemetry-bot: Note: recent telemetry config PR #512 added user email regex but only applied to log formatting.

maria: action items: trent -> node SDK change + test; li -> python SDK change + test; ryan -> canonical redaction config + docs snippet; i'll draft RFC with the API shape `telemetry: { redaction_rules: [], pre_process_span: optional_callable }`.

trent: will ping if I run into exporter timing issues (need pre-export hook to modify spans before gz + http send).

li: also add an example in sample-apps that demonstrates end-to-end: request header -> logs + exported spans show same `request_id`, no emails.

maria: thanks — let's try to get PRs open by EOD tomorrow. :rocket:

